{{/*
  deck — the reveal.js deck page shell.

  This is the single page internal/render.RenderDeck parses and executes to
  produce the served presentation. It is OFFLINE: every URL below points into
  the embedded assets.FS (served under /assets/…), never at a CDN or any
  network location.

  Embedding / access:
    The pages sub-tree is embedded by internal/assets and exposed as
    assets.DeckPage() (an fs.FS rooted here), so the file's path is
    "deck.html.tmpl". internal/render does, in effect:

      template.Must(template.ParseFS(assets.DeckPage(), "deck.html.tmpl"))

  Execution context (a struct or map[string]any supplying these keys):
    .Title       string        deck title for the document <title>.
                               Empty falls back to "kalide".
    .ThemeCSS    string        URL of the resolved theme stylesheet
                               (theme-registry Stylesheet, e.g.
                               "/assets/theme.css"). Empty falls back to
                               "/assets/theme.css".
    .Navigation  string        navigationMode passed straight through from
                               kalide.yaml `navigation`: "default", "linear"
                               or "grid". Empty falls back to "default".
    .Slides      template.HTML rendered slides: the outer <section> elements
                               internal/render built (letter slides already
                               nested as vertical stacks). Injected verbatim
                               into the .reveal > .slides container.

  This shell intentionally does NOT receive `.deck.properties` or `.slide`.
  Those reserved keys are part of the per-slide execution context supplied to
  slide layouts and section templates only (template-context,
  section-template-context); the deck page shell is parsed and executed once
  per deck with the four keys above, after every slide has already been
  rendered into .Slides, so it has no use for and never sees per-slide or
  deck-properties context.

  Hook slots (phase 7):
    Both "theme-css" and "live-reload" are named blocks, so a caller may
    override them with {{ define }} before parsing and without editing this
    file. "live-reload" is empty in phase 6; the phase-7 server injects its
    SSE client script there.

  Print / PDF:
    reveal.js 6.x handles ?print-pdf in core — the print styles are bundled in
    the embedded dist/reveal.css, there is no separate print plugin or
    stylesheet. Loading this page with ?print-pdf is the whole of print
    support.
*/}}

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ with .Title }}{{ . }}{{ else }}kalide{{ end }}</title>

  {{/* Embedded reveal.js base styles, then the resolved theme tokens. */}}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/reveal/dist/reset.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/reveal/dist/reveal.css">
  {{ block "theme-css" . }}{{ with .ThemeCSS }}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ . }}">{{ else }}<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css">{{ end }}{{ end }}

  {{/* Reveal.js applies the .reveal-viewport metrics to <html> once initialised. */}}
</head>
<body>
  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="slides">
      {{/* internal/render fills this container with the rendered slides. */}}
      {{ .Slides }}
    </div>
  </div>

  {{/* Embedded reveal.js core and the speaker-notes plugin (dist/plugin/notes.js). */}}
  <script src="/assets/reveal/dist/reveal.js"></script>
  <script src="/assets/reveal/dist/plugin/notes.js"></script>
  <script>
    Reveal.initialize({
      hash: true,
      navigationMode: "{{ if .Navigation }}{{ .Navigation }}{{ else }}default{{ end }}",
      plugins: [ RevealNotes ],
    });
  </script>

  {{/* Phase-7 live-reload client script is injected here; empty in phase 6. */}}
  {{ block "live-reload" . }}{{ end }}
</body>
</html>
